      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linn_Creek%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The original town of Linn Creek now lies beneath the waters of the Lake of the Ozarks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linn_Creek%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Construction of the Bagnell Dam that created the lake began on August 8, 1929.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linn_Creek%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "When the dam project flooded the original town, the county seat moved to the new town of Camdenton in 1931.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linn_Creek%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Linn Creek was first settled in 1841 at the junction of the Niangua and Osage Rivers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linn_Creek%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Linn Creek once served as a head of navigation on the Osage, becoming a major transportation hub in southwest Missouri.",
